# Shared surfaces (#231): a change to any path matched here takes a diff out of
# the quick flow at close, whatever its size — these are the seams other repos,
# issues and gates read, where a small edit has a large blast radius.
#
# The pattern forms (and the ones refused) are printed by `sdlc close --help`,
# under THE QUICK FLOW — that is their one statement. This file itself is always
# a shared surface, and close reads it as committed at the review window's base
# AND head, and on both sides of a rename, so a branch cannot loosen its shell by
# editing it. `sdlc change-code --help` prints the rest of the shell.

# The gate machinery itself. ariadne's sdlc is built from the checkout the branch
# lives in, so a quick branch that edited anything compiled into it — the shell's
# limits, its classifier, the close step, the review recipes, the frontmatter
# reader — would close under the binary it just changed. The gates do not change
# under the gate: every change to sdlc's build closure takes the full flow.
# TestRepoDeclarationCoversTheShell derives that closure (`go list -deps
# ./cmd/sdlc` within this module, embedded files included, plus every module-mode
# input: go.mod, go.sum, go.work*, vendor/) and requires every file to match.
cmd/sdlc/
pkg/
go.mod
go.sum
go.work
go.work.sum
vendor/

# The vocabulary models — every consumer derives from them (their Go embedding,
# pkg/vocab/, is in the build closure above).
construct/vocabulary/*.cue

# The base layer propagated to every downstream repo.
construct/base.manifest
AGENTS.base.md
